## 1. THE BIG IDEA FRAMEWORK

### 1.1 The Core Philosophy

Coatue's investment approach blends three disciplines:
- **"Big Fucking Ideas" (BFI)** — massive, multi-year technological paradigm shifts
- **Rigorous fundamental modeling** — "sacred" cell-by-cell financial models
- **Alternative data science** — joining disparate datasets to uncover hidden truths

**Philippe Laffont on his identity:** "I try to view myself as a growth investor. And I think a growth investor is someone who wants to be a value investor in ten years."

**Thomas Laffont on the firm's scope:** "We think more about innovation than tech." Coatue covers approximately 85% of the S&P.

### 1.2 BFI Selection Criteria

| Criterion | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Magnitude** | Multi-decade paradigm shifts, not 2-3 year trends |
| **TAM trajectory** | Market must grow 2-3x over 5-10 years AND allow TAM stacking |
| **Infrastructure necessity** | Prefer foundational layers (chips, data centers, power) over applications |
| **Diversifiable bet** | Must be able to build a basket within the trend — not a single-winner bet |
| **Survival horizon** | Can the capital survive 5+ years of development? |

**Thomas's framing:** "We're not going to have AI without semis so semis are kind of a foundational layer... we're going to need data centers and we're going to need power."

### 1.3 The AI Infrastructure Thesis — Layer Stack

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Layer 3: Applications & Data (Fuzziest)     │
│  Snowflake, Databricks, legacy SaaS          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
