## 3. TAM GROWTH & TAM STACKING

### 3.1 Ignore Static TAM

**Philippe's rule:** "When a founder pitches their TAM, I largely ignore it."

Two questions replace static TAM analysis:

| Question | What to Look For | Examples |
|----------|-----------------|----------|
| **Will the TAM grow?** | Markets that will organically expand 2x to 3x over 5-10 years | AI infrastructure, digital banking, satellite broadband |
| **Can the company stack additional TAMs?** | Businesses that layer entirely new markets onto their core product | Uber (rides → groceries → delivery), Apple (iPhone → services → wearables) |

### 3.2 TAM Stacking in Practice

| Company | Core TAM | Stacked TAMs |
|---------|----------|--------------|
| Apple | iPhone hardware | Services ($100B+), App Store, Wearables, iCloud |
| Uber | Ride-sharing | Uber Eats, Uber Grocery, Freight |
| OpenAI | Model API | ChatGPT subscription, Enterprise, Agent platforms |

**Thomas on Apple:** "They successfully added additional TAMs through services."

