## 7. STRUCTURING LUCK & PORTFOLIO CONSTRUCTION

### 7.1 The "Luck on Your Side" Principle

Instead of trying to pick ONE winner in a massive paradigm shift, Philippe prefers to build a portfolio where **"luck is on your side."**

**Example — AI as a utility:**
- Knowing intelligence will become the next great global utility
- Own a diversified basket of foundational AI companies (OpenAI + Anthropic + Google)
- Captures the upside regardless of which specific model wins

### 7.2 Cash Management

**Philippe's approach to cash:**
- "There are times where we've held 80% cash in our fund"
- "My highest conviction idea is to decide what your risk tolerance is. And it could be 0% of your portfolio all the way up to 100"
- Extreme cash positions are a risk management tool, not a sign of bearishness

### 7.3 Sector Diversification

Coatue covers ~85% of the S&P but thinks in terms of **innovation sectors:**

| Sector | View |
|--------|------|
| **AI / Semis** | Highest conviction — infrastructure first |
| **Fintech** | Highly bullish — digitization of banking (Revolut as potential trillion-dollar digital JPMorgan) |
| **Space** | Telecom disruption — satellite broadband has "very bad implications" for terrestrial wireless and cable |
| **Stablecoins** | Core conviction — predicts U.S. government will issue yield-bearing stablecoins directly to consumers |
| **Crypto/meme coins** | Negative — Philippe openly says he's "Negative Bitcoin" despite schizophrenic FOMO |

