## 11. WORKFLOW & DECISION PROCESS

### 11.1 The Coatue Workflow

```
Idea Generation (BFI scanning)
        ↓
Initial Pitch (any team member)
        ↓
Radical, Immediate Collaboration
  ├─ Public team analysts chime in immediately
  ├─ Private team analysts chime in immediately
  └─ Iterate thesis in real-time
        ↓
Build "Sacred" Financial Model (cell-by-cell)
        ↓
Reverse-Engineer Bear/Bull Case (test assumptions)
        ↓
Apply Universal Opportunity Cost (compare vs 5% RFR + Mag 7)
        ↓
Three-Sentence Thesis Test (Spielberg Rule)
        ↓
Decide: Invest / Pass / More Research
        ↓
If Invest: Position size based on risk tolerance
        ↓
Ongoing: Mental flexibility — force reverse-engineering when stuck
```

### 11.2 No Traditional Investment Committee

**Thomas's anti-pattern:** "We actively avoid the classic venture capital model of a top-down, 'wise men' investment committee where analysts wait for the smoke to go up the chimney."

Instead:
- Deals are decided through **internal momentum**
- **Radical, immediate collaboration** — when a private software idea is pitched, the firm's public market software analyst is expected to chime in immediately
- This lets the team iterate and improve the thesis in real-time

### 11.3 Testing Assumptions

**Thomas's method:**
- Force analysts to articulate both bull AND bear cases
- Whichever side the analyst argues, Thomas argues the opposite to expose blind spots
- Actively recruit "tiger parents" and practitioners of radical candor to provide brutal feedback

**Philippe's method:**
- When stuck in a bearish mindset: force reverse-engineering of the bull case
- Ask: "Why do many people in the market think it's worth 2 trillion? What is it they see that I don't?"

