## 15. THE 20-CRITERIA INVESTMENT RUBRIC

### Scoring Scale

| Level | Label | Description |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| **1** | Novice | Detrimental analysis, wrong frameworks |
| **2** | Basic | Standard tools, surface-level |
| **3** | Proficient | Competent analysis, some insight |
| **4** | Advanced | Deep expertise, multiple frameworks |
| **5** | Laffont Mastery | BFI-level thinking, data science, three-sentence clarity |

### The 20 Criteria

| # | Criterion | Level 1 | Level 3 | Level 5 |
|---|-----------|---------|---------|---------|
| 1 | **Core Trend Identification** | Focuses on small static niches | Targets existing well-defined large markets | Exclusively targets "Big Fucking Ideas" (BFIs) capable of multi-decade paradigm shifts |
| 2 | **TAM Evaluation** | Accepts founder's static TAM pitch | Models moderate linear TAM expansion | Ignores static TAM entirely; evaluates if TAM can grow 2-3x AND stack additional TAMs |
| 3 | **Financial Modeling** | Relies on thousand-line sell-side models | Builds standard models with conventional lines | Builds models cell-by-cell as "sacred" spaces; ruthlessly eliminates non-thesis-driving lines |
| 4 | **Thesis Clarity** | Ramble, multi-page explanations | Short paragraph summary | Applies Spielberg's three-sentence script rule — pitch stock's essence in exactly 3 sentences |
| 5 | **Data Science Strategy** | Standard quarterly reports only | Basic single-source alt data | Joins completely disparate datasets (credit card + email receipts) to uncover non-obvious shifts |
| 6 | **Mental Flexibility** | Dogmatic, refuses to change mind | Acknowledges opposing views exist | Forces reverse-engineering of opposite perspective; tests own assumptions aggressively |
| 7 | **Risk Management** | Zero-sum betting with no protection | Basic diversification | "Survival paranoia" — uses hedges and 80% cash positions to endure decades |
| 8 | **Portfolio "Luck" Structuring** | Bet on one winner per trend | Picks a few names in a sector | Builds diversified basket within mega-trend to capture upside regardless of which company wins |
| 9 | **Market Agnosticism** | Stays only in VC or public | Occasional crossover | Treats public/private fluidly — "fisherman" seeking best value up and down the river |
| 10 | **Index Independence** | Surrenders to MSCI/S&P | Slight over/underweight | Completely reinvents index weights based on future utilities 5-10 years out |
| 11 | **Investment Horizon** | Short-term trading | 3-5 year outlook | Growth investor today with explicit goal of being value investor in same asset in 10 years |
| 12 | **Private Company Strategy** | Evaluates on hype alone | Considers growth vs burn | Strict 25% growth/profitability matrix dictating IPO readiness, fortress balance sheet, or reinvention |
| 13 | **Leadership Assessment** | 1990s GE charisma | Standard management skills | Extreme adaptability, survival instinct, hands-on debugging, and "star quality" magnetism |
| 14 | **Efficiency / "Get Fit"** | Massive hiring sprees | Linear headcount-to-revenue | AI-powered: double revenue while shrinking headcount |
| 15 | **Collaborative Diligence** | Siloed investment committee | Occasional check-ins | Radical immediate collaboration across public/private teams for unstoppable momentum |
| 16 | **Public Scrutiny & IPOs** | Stay private indefinitely | Neutral on IPO timing | Champions public market as "great disinfectant" — forces discipline, tests true value |
| 17 | **Attention to Detail** | Sloppy analysis | Clean but unfocused | "Gift wrapping" — every cell, font, color serves specific narrative purpose |
| 18 | **Product & GTM Symbiosis** | Great product sells itself | Product and sales siloed | Product and sales as identical sides of same coin — positioning before roadmap |
| 19 | **Macro Perspective** | Ignores macro entirely | Paralyzed by macro fears | Contextualizes structural fears — can tech productivity outgrow sovereign debt cycles? |
| 20 | **Seeking Critical Feedback** | Sycophants confirm biases | Polite board feedback | Actively recruits "tiger parents" and radical candor to expose blind spots |

